subQuestions.prompt:
A cocoa farmer shared a tract of farmland among his three children. The first child received $\frac{2}{5}$ of the land, and the second child received 6 acres more than the first child. The third child was given the remaining 18 acres. Find:
(i) the total acres of land shared;
(ii) the number of acres received by the first child;
(iii) the number of acres received by the second child.

From your graph in (a), determine:
(i) the distance from the service station to Town B;
(ii) the total time (in minutes) taken for the whole journey including the rest period;
(iii) the average speed of the truck from the service station to Town B in km/h.
